swer/id #uuid "af1d9e98-01ee-5e09-a40e-c6c7536cf1e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af1d9e98-01ee-5e09-a40e-c6c7536cf1e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526273} :answer-field/id #uuid "b368afd7-11d1-5171-91a6-711599734482" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc109745-8355-56e8-af55-b73e86b9345e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc109745-8355-56e8-af55-b73e86b9345e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526278} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d5dc46-4c4c-5255-98ec-05bafc71b2aa" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526276} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02512a09-5ac5-52dc-9b5a-afdf34c262fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02512a09-5ac5-52dc-9b5a-afdf34c262fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526228} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfa249a-be73-5c4c-a780-716646abeb3f" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d6d715d-38c8-5b0a-b2d3-582f990f1069" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -\\frac{5}{2},\\,y=-\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +\\frac{1}{3},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}}{{field-2}}$x\\le ${{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}}$\\le y${{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta\\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4} & \\le -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{5}{2} & \\le -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -\\frac{5}{2}\\le \\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{4} & \\le x\\le -\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{15}{4}\\le x\\le -\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta\\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} & \\le -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{1}{3} & \\le -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +\\frac{1}{3}\\le \\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{25}{6} & \\le y\\le \\frac{29}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{25}{6}\\le y\\le \\frac{29}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c435b2-8b4b-52dc-aa07-5619c250e68e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}-y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526379} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4e14c2-2018-5557-b5ae-6da902977c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526380} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c4c55a-37ab-5244-9e53-604e66dac006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526382} {:answer/id #uuid "d32cc603-e58c-5b00-a8b9-0a073ffc01e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526383} {:answer/id #uuid "d97f9dc5-21b6-5ee0-a46c-0f9f54098a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}-y^{2}=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4e14c2-2018-5557-b5ae-6da902977c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526380} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad8a1cf2-3368-5b81-80d2-fd8f9646b9dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eaf5e3f7-8e64-5b18-999b-2cd25904a7b4" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta.$ We can do this using the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.$$\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta\\\\x^2&=(\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta)^2\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta\\\\y^2&=(\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta)^2\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using the identity, we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^2+y^2&=\\frac{121}{4}\\cos^2\\theta+\\frac{121}{4}\\sin^2\\theta\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}(1)\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28030418-5f24-5272-86ce-e3723aabb231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526399} {:answer/id #uuid "58bcd153-e4a6-5347-b974-b9ed5dc0fe90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526414} {:answer/id #uuid "628cb4c0-5057-556d-a14c-1a38c916f6bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526416} {:answer/id #uuid "837ec4f1-2785-5592-84e2-6ce366787415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526425} {:answer/id #uuid "d1406d71-acc3-535d-9583-aa1c7ab89832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1406d71-acc3-535d-9583-aa1c7ab89832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526451} :answer-field/id #uuid "02eb60d5-5312-5ccf-8a81-9bea45dbebe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e7676fd-d001-5de3-b465-0aeb6e24740a" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} + x y$ and $y=- \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f719175-0350-5ab1-8b31-b6444a8164e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526411} {:answer/id #uuid "564ef5c0-2148-5813-bea6-ba25040c8f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526413} {:answer/id #uuid "5df99349-f91f-5ae1-99b2-bcd6b3fc1586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526415} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0cd494-6b02-58ed-8cc8-2b861c96e086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526420} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8b0928-aa99-59cc-92d0-19375c21d27c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5df99349-f91f-5ae1-99b2-bcd6b3fc1586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526415} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f324d52-4c30-5c1d-bb2a-4a9f0a9dcf71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72cc3095-5d1d-534f-8f85-48cfe2429d46" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} - 2 x y$ and $y=- \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x - 2 y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 2 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\\\  & =2 \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1252db4f-6351-5996-b74d-6d5bf42f331e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526395} {:answer/id #uuid "2a485976-4f67-547b-b3d2-f48f0f3d4189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526401} {:answer/id #uuid "7f6fd225-cc83-5dab-bacf-849050e741c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526424} {:answer/id #uuid "88241d4f-b699-51c6-a094-8e175af83201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526428} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd3c03e-062b-5987-afd5-25a75a4ff6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccd3c03e-062b-5987-afd5-25a75a4ff6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526450} :answer-field/id #uuid "54c6b567-0bd7-5bb7-9bc9-1e721afcf635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d1cf1af-73f0-5835-a9c0-2ae46945e41a" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + x y$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=8 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8d57-eed3-5f7f-803c-e4b08b5a2fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526394} {:answer/id #uuid "487c1d4a-c93e-5489-bccb-93e33859361b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526408} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8680f2-cbde-55a5-95b1-4d2e08e21b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526409} {:answer/id #uuid "7387c28f-4867-5085-b7c6-81bc1baa6e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526418} {:answer/id #uuid "e99a6ce9-68cd-5ec0-ab4c-c9f8479a2750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a8680f2-cbde-55a5-95b1-4d2e08e21b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526409} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd71c7d-3950-511e-bbd6-2df993c0ae98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f57aa56-b41b-566d-8ea7-a684dfb21253" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 x e^{- 3 y}$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=2 e^{- 3 y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 6 x e^{- 3 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}+\\left(- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\\\  & =- 2 \\left(12 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 1\\right) e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424393bd-012e-5487-b5fa-2d9b39260b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526407} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b23c9a-7d39-54a4-a0c2-ebe6cb589e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526435} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cf6f21-2a5f-5fbe-af69-59ade2a54030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 x \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526436} {:answer/id #uuid "af678b84-5edb-5546-b998-af5d8656b803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x^{2} e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526439} {:answer/id #uuid "d4672b92-b3c7-54b8-80c8-31f3d94077aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4672b92-b3c7-54b8-80c8-31f3d94077aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526452} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1fc4e7e-ffc1-5cf5-8a0e-e7ccfe76dda1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "84520ae9-d161-55be-8813-c4f436891538" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 x e^{- 3 y}$ and $y=x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=2 e^{- 3 y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 6 x e^{- 3 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1x) & =1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}) & =- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}+\\left(- 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =24 x^{2} e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\\\  & =2 \\left(12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186bfece-020c-5fef-8ded-f89e7e7c948a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x^{2} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526397} {:answer/id #uuid "2936b0cb-ae36-59c0-b3e1-1f34022918b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526400} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9e9f8a-10b2-597f-898d-54d7713ef86d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526402} {:answer/id #uuid "419ef840-0342-58fd-96ed-e9251fe88f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526406} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5d9c50-a79b-57ab-af34-2bdd942f4a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "419ef840-0342-58fd-96ed-e9251fe88f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526406} :answer-field/id #uuid "a06eaab3-3b05-5df8-b761-4fca2b88c718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "944dba1d-61e2-5ad6-8d02-a9d420bedc5f" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} + x y$ and $y=- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-1x) & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}) & =4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\cdot \\left(\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(-1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x \\\\  & =- 2 x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526441 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3efe972a-ae63-59cc-951a-d997c172f209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526405} {:answer/id #uuid "9006440e-db82-5fc3-92bd-e5850a7af94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526429} {:answer/id #u